{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/97546-fictitious-pantheons","id":97546,"title":"Fictitious Pantheons","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-24T08:42:04-07:00","id":97546,"title":"Fictitious Pantheons","content":"What is your opinion of them? Would you or do you use one in your game; whether for player characters or &quot;villains&quot;? If so, who are the gods? A version of American/Yankee gods or maybe the Great Old Ones from HP Lovecraft or one completely from your own imagination? And as a follow up if you have run or participated in a campaign where a fictitious pantheon was employed how did it turn out?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Every normal man must be tempted at times to spit upon his hands, hoist the black flag, and begin slitting throats.&quot;<br /> -H.L. Mencken","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2486-irisheathen","name":"Irisheathen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2486_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T09:39:30-07:00","id":97573,"title":"","content":"Well, I turned some of the HPL great old ones into a form of corrupt titanic avatar as the result of Hundun's interference. Made for some decent enough villains at God level who had no ambiguity about how freaking evil they were. Everyone who even suggests the idea using fictitious pantheons for PCs seems to get carpet-bombed with flames.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T12:21:03-07:00","id":97656,"title":"","content":"It really depends. For the base game probably a bad idea unless you are trying to show of younger pantheons that may have popped up since mythical times. If you want to shift the tone of the game though fictional pantheons can get some real mileage. What fictional pantheons you use really depends on what you are trying to accomplish though. Take for example I think it might be really cool to run a game in a D&amp;D setting but use Scion rules. This would require that I build the settings pantheon, probably a few outside forces as well to describe characters less strongly associated with the gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T13:16:07-07:00","id":97696,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of Pantheons based on new age religions - not fantasy (sorry Lovecraft) but stuff like Wiccia being explicitly founded by Scions trying to create beliefs more in-line with modern values.<br /> <br /> Pantheons based on something other than a real religion, not for me. With an exception for the Vanguard of Avalon. That one was pretty sweet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T13:44:17-07:00","id":97720,"title":"","content":"The Aztecs were kicking around less than 500 years ago. The Deva, Orisha, and Shen are kicking around right now. There are so many non-fictitious pantheons you could put in your game, I do not even know why you would bother with a fictitious one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T16:30:13-07:00","id":97849,"title":"","content":"The challenge of something fresh perhaps? It does fire the imagination a bit to create something new.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T21:28:07-07:00","id":98064,"title":"","content":"Ehh... I've never really seen a truly unique fictional Pantheon that really made me say &quot;Yes, this is totally awesome and feels like it could really have existed as a religion at some point&quot;. If I wanted to play fantasy games, there are way better systems than Scion to do it in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T22:29:15-07:00","id":98088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/97546-fictitious-pantheons?p=97849#post97849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The challenge of something fresh perhaps? It does fire the imagination a bit to create something new.</div> </div> </div> </div>Scion is a game about mythology. If someone does not want mythology in their game, I could recommend Mutants &amp; Masterminds as an excellent system for playing fictional characters. Usually people love the idea of Scion, and merely cope / house rule the mechanics. However, I suppose it is possible for someone to love the mechanics of Scion so much that they want to extend them to non-mythology. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T09:28:38-07:00","id":98412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/97546-fictitious-pantheons?p=98088#post98088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scion is a game about mythology. If someone does not want mythology in their game, I could recommend Mutants &amp; Masterminds as an excellent system for playing fictional characters. Usually people love the idea of Scion, and merely cope / house rule the mechanics. However, I suppose it is possible for someone to love the mechanics of Scion so much that they want to extend them to non-mythology. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>So first off unless you've seen Zeus recently I would say most pantheons could be called fictional in the grand scheme of things. As for merely coping for the mythology and setting I'm sure you could find other systems that work better. For what ever reasons we have all chosen this setting with this system even if we do have to use house rules. Finally I personally have created pantheons to use as antagonists simply to give my players something new to face. I know I could use the aztlanti but why not use the great old ones with hidden cults around the globe? Its a choice well all get to make as Story Tellers and that's fine if you don't want to; but please don't look down your nose at innocent creativity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Every normal man must be tempted at times to spit upon his hands, hoist the black flag, and begin slitting throats.&quot;<br /> -H.L. Mencken","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2486-irisheathen","name":"Irisheathen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2486_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T10:02:45-07:00","id":98431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irisheathen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/97546-fictitious-pantheons?p=98412#post98412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So first off unless you've seen Zeus recently I would say most pantheons could be called fictional in the grand scheme of things</div> </div> </div> </div>Telling people their religion is fictional rarely has a good outcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T10:39:06-07:00","id":98467,"title":"","content":"Done with this. I want to run a tabletop RPG not have philosophical debates. PS until it has proof behind it it is fiction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Every normal man must be tempted at times to spit upon his hands, hoist the black flag, and begin slitting throats.&quot;<br /> -H.L. Mencken","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2486-irisheathen","name":"Irisheathen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2486_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T12:06:30-07:00","id":98545,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>This forum has followers of a number of religions. Expressing Atheism or Agnosticism is fine, but referring to them as all fiction is needlessly dismissive.</b></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T14:45:45-07:00","id":98674,"title":"","content":"I think the point of referring to Scion as having a basis in mythology is to emphasize its nature as a collision between the ancient and the modern. While many deities espoused in Scion are still worshipped, most of them came into being much earlier. I don't have any problem with using something like the Great Old Ones in a game, BUT I would never explicitly use the same things that HP Lovecraft used. I would use more generic &quot;dangerous beings beyond our conceptualization of time and space&quot;. To do so would imply one of two things, neither of which I think are particularly good: A) that Lovecraft (and his successors, eg Derleth) were somehow clued-in on the true nature of the setting, or B) that a text that hasn't been particularly widely read has brought such beings into existence. Which of the two is true depends on your particular metaphysics in your particular Scion games, but I'm not a fan of either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T04:33:16-07:00","id":99914,"title":"","content":"Although Lovecraft was creating fictions, his Great Old Ones are very much shaped by Mythology. The versions of the deities used in the actual Scion game are likewise fictions based on Mythology (although I assume most of the deities involved would have a sense of humor about the whole thing). Certain fictions (Lovercraft, Tolkien, ect) are created from mythology with great creativity and respect, these seem to me like reasonable sources for game fodder. Other fictions are less creative and/or respectful and would be less congruent. Indiviual game groups can decide these things for themselves.<br /> <br /> Also, certain games would logically rework pantheons in fictional ways. Say you have a game set on a Terraformed world orbiting a star 400 lyrs from Earth in the year 12000AD. You might rework several patheons or introduce new ones with ancient roots. It's a matter of taste.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}